      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright 2010 Mosby, Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "Aplasia of the major salivary glands is a very uncommon anomaly, with isolated aplasia of only 1 submandibular gland being even rarer. We report a case of a 60-year-old woman in whom unilateral aplasia of the left submandibular gland was detected incidentally on computerized tomography with no other associated congenital abnormalities."
      },
